 number.\n\n- **If** $2$ is an even number, **then** $3$ is an even number.\n\n- **If** $2$ is an odd number, **then** $3$ is an odd number." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059406 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "13e5834d-4d70-5893-a4bf-9927000d522d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059406 #edb/ref 1074 "An implication $A \\Rightarrow B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. In other words, the implication is true unless the \"promise\" is broken.\n\n- Statement I is true. The antecedent \"$2$ is an even number\" is true, and the consequent \"$3$ is an odd number\" is true. So the promise is kept, and the statement is true.\n\n- Statement II is false. The antecedent \"$2$ is an even number\" is true, and the consequent \"$3$ is an even number\" is false. So the promise is broken, and the statement is false.\n\n- Statement III is true. The antecedent \"$2$ is an odd number\" is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059407 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12705" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059407 #edb/ref 1071 "What are the missing values in the following truth table?\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\, \\neg A \\Rightarrow (A \\land B) \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\phantom{F}}$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\phantom{F}}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\phantom{F}}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\phantom{F}}$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059407 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0b97d670-694b-52e5-aa55-1224985f83a8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059407 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we add columns for $\\neg A$ and $A \\land B{:}$\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\, \\neg A \\,$ | $\\, A \\land B \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n\nNow, we add a column for $\\neg A \\Rightarrow (A \\land B).$ This statement is true unless $\\neg A$ is true and $A \\land B$ is false.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\, \\neg A \\,$ | $\\, A \\land B \\,$ | $\\, \\neg A \\Rightarrow (A \\land B) \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059408 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12706" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059408 #edb/ref 1071 "If $A$ is true, then $A \\Rightarrow B$ is $\\text{______________}.$\n\nWhich of the following could fill in the blank space above to make a true statement?\n\n- always true\n\n- always false\n\n- sometimes false" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059408 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8831a019-f252-5678-9855-6c0f1da89f77" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059408 #edb/ref 1074 "The statement $A \\Rightarrow B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. \n\nLet's break this down into cases:\n\n- When $A = \\textrm T$ and $B = \\textrm T,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A⇒B) & ≡(\\text{T}⇒\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $A = \\textrm T$ and $B = \\textrm F,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A⇒B) & ≡(\\text{T}⇒\\text{F}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $A$ is true, then $A \\Rightarrow B$ is $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm{sometimes false}}.$\n\nThe complete truth table for $A\\Rightarrow B$ is shown below:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A \\Rightarrow B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059699 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186060135 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059699 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186060136 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059699 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186376268 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059699 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186376274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059699 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186376292 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059699 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186376302 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059699 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186572129 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059699 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying Truth Values of Implications" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059699 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186059408 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059699 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "df9791a3-465d-57e4-8f2e-40fb9fb18d70" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059700 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050777 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059700 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186060137 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059700 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186060151 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059700 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186060152 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059700 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186376388 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059700 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186376401 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059700 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186390071 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059700 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186390113 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059700 #edb/re