b/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186059124 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060417 #edb/ref 1069 "q-82070" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060417 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060417 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. **If** $5$ is a prime number, **then** $4$ is a composite number.\n2. **If** $4$ is a prime number, **then** $5$ is a composite number.\n3. **If** $5$ is a prime number, **then** $4$ is a prime number." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060417 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "50077fd5-22af-5609-98e0-9c3d33888ef9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060569 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186060570 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060569 #edb/ref 1061 154035 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060569 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "62e05d8d-2ee3-5cd5-8592-01e6eef66d71" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060569 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186060983 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060570 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186060571 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060570 #edb/ref 1061 154036 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060570 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "89220a35-670a-5c3b-9161-aa844a949880" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060570 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186059699 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060571 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186060572 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060571 #edb/ref 1061 154039 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060571 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cb82b9e6-f25a-5610-8374-2261c53cde3b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060571 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186059700 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060572 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186060573 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060572 #edb/ref 1061 154043 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060572 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4b3b0e3b-bca5-585d-999e-a2ea88c36b2b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060572 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186060994 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060573 #edb/ref 1061 154044 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060573 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ea087540-046f-51b4-a818-16971088b6d6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060573 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186059701 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060983 #edb/ref 1064 "A **conditional statement** (or **implication**) is a mathematical statement that takes the form \n\n$\\qquad$ *$P$ implies $Q,$* \n\nor equivalently, \n\n$\\qquad$ *if $P,$ then $Q.$*\n\nSymbolically, it can be written as $P \\Rightarrow Q,$ where $P$ is called the **antecedent** (or **hypothesis**) and $Q$ is called the **consequent** (or **conclusion**).\n\nThe truth table for $P \\Rightarrow Q$ is shown below.\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\, P \\Rightarrow Q \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm T$ |\n\nIntuitively, an implication can be viewed as a \"promise\" that whenever $P$ is true, $Q$ is also true. The implication is true unless the promise is broken, i.e., $P$ is true, and $Q$ is false. \n\nWe'll discuss the intuition behind implications in more detail later in the lesson." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060983 #edb/ref 1065 7977 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060983 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "a6598728-1780-50b5-af45-ace426318bc6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060983 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060994 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's recall the truth table for $P\\Rightarrow Q.$\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\, P \\Rightarrow Q \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm T$ |\n\nWe consider a concrete example to build further intuition behind the truth values in this table.\n\nSuppose your teacher promises that *if* you score at least $90$ on the exam, *then* you will receive an A. In other words, the teacher has promised that a score of at least $90$ on the exam implies that you will receive an A: \n![](images/d4/d4f1e90fe7e41304a17495224494b8860951877c22c58905f59f4580d067469e.svg)\n\nNow, the teacher may or may not be lying. The implication is true if the teacher tells the truth and false if the teacher lies. \n\nThe following four situations are possible:\n\n1\\. You score $90$ and receive an A. In this case, the teacher has told the truth. They have kept the promise. $\\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n\n2\\. You score $90$ and do *not* receive an A. In this case, the teacher has lied. They have broken the promise. $\\quad \\color{red}\\times$\n\n3\\. You do *not* score $90,$ yet you receive an A. In this case, the teacher has told the truth! The promise does not apply because you did not score at least $90.$ $\\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n\n4\\. You do *not* score $90$ and do *not* receive an A. Again, the teacher has told the truth. The promise does not apply because you did not score at least $90.$ $\\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n\nEach of these situations corresponds to a row in the following truth table:\n\n| ![](images/eb/ebffdf1820c35f70b5ab8325025bd413889c37eb3daec640f273eb6046808182.svg) | $\\textrm{Receive an A}$ | ![](images/e9/e94a03764a9e6c587b69756d54780679195290cf9b19c12df187194a009fc880.svg) |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm T$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060994 #edb/ref 1065 8292 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060994 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "6943ab9c-bf27-5dbb-9871-a5647b7d3b74" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060994 #edb/ref 1067 "Intuition Behind the Implication Truth Table" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376268 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186376269 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376268 #edb/ref 1069 "q-182489" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376268 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376268 #edb/ref 1071 "If $A$ is false and $B$ is true, then $A⇒B$ is{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376268 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6582d0eb-c820-55a9-aa44-17c726abba33" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376268 #edb/ref 1074 "The statement $A⇒B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. \n\nSo, when $A=\\text{F}$ and $B=\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A⇒B) & ≡(\\text{F}⇒\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe complete truth table for $A⇒B$ is shown below:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A⇒B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376269 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186376270 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376269 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186376271 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376269 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186376272 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376269 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186376273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376269 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376269 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376269 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186376273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376269 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "0cbf9a7f-6130-5a5e-83ff-392722284603" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376270 #edb/ref 1080 "sometimes false" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376270 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376270 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6e9c7bbf-fb00-539d-87b4-f3bc2523bc2a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376271 #edb/ref 1080 "sometimes true" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376271 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376271 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e3a30bad-0f59-53be-afc3-27600bac37ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376272 #edb/ref 1080 "always false" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376272 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376272 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b2bf29ad-0150-5ba4-9be4-c00ede5f44d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376273 #edb/ref 1080 "always true" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376273 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376273 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ad50e2aa-6971-51a4-b3e5-cdf1c9a45d84" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376274 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186376275 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376274 #edb/ref 1069 "q-182491" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376274 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376274 #edb/ref 1071 "If $A$ is true, then $A⇒B$ is{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376274 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "606e4737-3efc-59b1-bc9c-91c798e9d0e5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376274 #edb/ref 1074 "The statement $A⇒B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. \n\nLet's break this down into cases:\n\n- When $A=\\text{T}$ and $B=\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A⇒B) & ≡(\\text{T}⇒\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $A=\\text{T}$ and $B=\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A⇒B) & ≡(\\text{T}⇒\\text{F}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $A$ is true, then $A⇒B$ is $\\text{sometimes true}.$\n\nThe complete truth table for $A⇒B$ is shown below:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A⇒B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376275 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186376276 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376275 #edb/ref 10